1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,733
You already know what you want to make.

2
00:00:01,733 --> 00:00:04,467
The hard part is getting the software to understand it.

3
00:00:04,633 --> 00:00:11,267
Traditional creative tools ask you to learn a cockpit of layers, panels, coordinates,

4
00:00:11,267 --> 00:00:13,133
and hidden rules before you can shape the idea.

5
00:00:13,133 --> 00:00:14,933
One-shot creative agents promise a shortcut,

6
00:00:14,933 --> 00:00:17,267
but when they cannot reach the real canvas, they still hand back a guess.

7
00:00:17,700 --> 00:00:18,533
Meant changes that.

8
00:00:18,933 --> 00:00:21,067
This isn’t a chatbot sitting beside your work.

9
00:00:21,500 --> 00:00:26,533
With WebMCP, the agent works on the same selected object, inside the same artifact,

10
00:00:26,533 --> 00:00:29,600
through the same bounded creative tools you use.

11
00:00:30,133 --> 00:00:33,067
You describe the outcome in your own words, and the idea takes shape

12
00:00:33,067 --> 00:00:36,367
where you can see it, touch it, and continue shaping it.

13
00:00:37,133 --> 00:00:39,000
Every proposal begins in Exploring.

14
00:00:39,500 --> 00:00:40,733
It appears on the canvas, but it stays temporary.

15
00:00:41,200 --> 00:00:46,000
You can refine it conversationally, compare it beside the version you already trust,

16
00:00:46,000 --> 00:00:49,333
or discard it without disturbing your kept work.

17
00:00:50,900 --> 00:00:53,167
When a direction feels right, choose Keep.

18
00:00:53,433 --> 00:00:56,100
Meant saves that exact result as a durable revision.

19
00:00:56,133 --> 00:00:58,333
If you change your mind, choose Undo.

20
00:00:58,367 --> 00:01:01,733
Meant restores the earlier result without erasing what happened.

21
00:01:02,200 --> 00:01:04,800
History preserves both the change and the recovery,

22
00:01:04,833 --> 00:01:07,900
so you never have to trade experimentation for control.

23
00:01:08,500 --> 00:01:10,567
The agent can inspect, create, and propose.

24
00:01:10,900 --> 00:01:12,967
It can ask to Keep, Discard, or Undo.

25
00:01:13,167 --> 00:01:16,000
You make the consequential decision, and Meant records it visibly.

26
00:01:18,633 --> 00:01:20,300
That changes the creative process.

27
00:01:20,300 --> 00:01:23,967
You spend less time translating intent into interface mechanics.

28
00:01:23,967 --> 00:01:26,967
You can explore more directions without losing the good ones.

29
00:01:26,967 --> 00:01:29,633
And instead of accepting a flattened answer,

30
00:01:29,633 --> 00:01:31,967
you shape the real artifact through conversation.

31
00:01:31,967 --> 00:01:34,967
The distance between what you imagine and what you can make gets shorter.

32
00:01:34,967 --> 00:01:36,800
Your idea stays visible.

33
00:01:36,800 --> 00:01:37,800
Every decision stays yours.

34
00:01:39,533 --> 00:01:41,333
Meant. Make what you mean.

